WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.040
JEN: Today, we're talking about
VM migration, custom voice,

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.690
and disaster recovery.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:07.910
I'm Jen, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.680
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.070
Google Cloud VMware Engine
helps simplify your migration

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.360
to Google Cloud.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.000
The service provides a
dedicated, software-defined

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.270
data center that allows you to
continue to use the core VMware

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:25.450
applications you need to run
your business in the cloud

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.680
without changes to your
tools, processes, or policies.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.850
In a recent survey by IDC, they
found that 78% of businesses

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.510
realized payback in one year
or less after they migrate.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.230
Learn how to maximize
your returns on the blog.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:44.650
We are excited to announce the
general availability of custom

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.380
voice in our Cloud
text-to-speech API,

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.660
a new feature that lets
you train custom voice

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.610
models with your
own audio recordings

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.250
to create customized
experiences.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.260
For businesses looking to
build a strong brand identity,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.100
this is a game changer
for customer experiences.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.830
Check out the blog for supported
languages and more detail.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.400
There are many reasons why
locality restrictions need

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.310
to be taken into consideration,
and it's something chief

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.980
information security
officers and resiliency

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.440
officers need to factor in.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.810
A balance needs to be met
between taking advantage

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.490
of your best
features of the cloud

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.740
while meeting your
locality requirements.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.740
Google Cloud helps you meet
your business's objectives,

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.140
whether your architecture
is all in on Google

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.800
Cloud, a hybrid pattern which
may be on-premises and Google

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:35.530
Cloud, or on Google Cloud and
an alternative cloud provider.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.810
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:40.220
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.470
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.250
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:46.080
We'll see you in the cloud.

